Then I could easily track the problem with

bash-3.2$ grep --color='auto' -P -n "[\x80-\xFF]" GenABEL/man/cocohet.Rd
29:Albert Hofman, Andr?? G. Uitterlinden, Yurii S. Aulchenko, and Manfred

(thanks to StackOverflow post
http://stackoverflow.com/questions/3001177/how-do-i-grep-for-non-ascii-characters-in-unix
)

best wishes,
Yurii



